# --- Repo-local additions (mission "REMOVE THE HUMAN FROM BEAM
# OPERATIONS", packaging follow-up, 2026-09-01) ---
# `beam deploy` was collecting 2.64 GB per deploy despite the patterns
# above, because none of them cover this repo's OWN large directories -
# `.venv`/`.git`/`node_modules` were already excluded but were NOT the
# real offenders here (confirmed via `du -sh`): `.router/` (Router/Remote
# Work worktree infrastructure, 2.1-3.5 GB depending on active worktrees)
# and `.claude/worktrees/` (381 MB) dominated the payload, with
# `web/node_modules` (749 MB, already covered by `**/node_modules/` above)
# and `web/public` (48 MB) contributing the rest.
#
# Confirmed SAFE to exclude everything below: grepped BOTH deployed apps'
# imports (beam_apps/translation_hymt2_app.py imports only `beam.
# integrations`; beam_apps/cover_illustrious_app.py imports only `beam`
# and its own sibling `cover_illustrious_logic` - both entirely within
# `beam_apps/`) - NEITHER app has a single import reaching outside
# `beam_apps/`, so nothing else in this repo is needed at Beam runtime.
# `beam_apps/` itself (and everything actually imported by it) is
# deliberately NOT listed here.
.router
.claude/worktrees
web
server
scripts
desktop_app
capcut_tts_api
tests
docs
deploy
examples
assets
.github
beam_apps/tests
legacy_gradio_app.py
